@startuml MassagePaw_UseCases
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName Monospace
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam shadowing false

title MassagePaw — Use Case Diagram (SysMLv2)\nuse case def — actors are «actor» features of the subject

' SysMLv2 use case syntax used in model:
'   use case def <Name> { subject, actor, objective doc, include use case <name>:<UC> }
' Actors appear as classifier roles, not standalone classifier boxes.

left to right direction

actor "operator : Person"  as Op
actor "recipient : Person" as Re

rectangle "subject: HeadMassageTeleOpSystem" {

  usecase "CalibrateSystem\n«use case def»\nObjective: Establish joint zeros\nand verify haptic loop." as UC1

  usecase "PerformHeadMassage\n«use case def»\nObjective: Operator guides robot\nhand through scalp massage strokes.\ninclude use case calibrate:CalibrateSystem" as UC2

  usecase "EmergencyStop\n«use case def»\nObjective: Halt and retract\nhand from contact." as UC3

  usecase "ForceLimitViolation\n«use case def»\nObjective: Safety module detects\nforce > 5 N, overrides command.\ninclude use case estop:EmergencyStop" as UC4

  usecase "AdjustTechnique\n(via ROS2 param)\nmassage_technique parameter" as UC5
}

Op  --> UC1
Op  --> UC2
Op  --> UC3
Op  --> UC5
Re  --> UC2

UC2 .> UC1 : <<include>>\ncalibrate : CalibrateSystem
UC4 .> UC3 : <<include>>\nestop : EmergencyStop
UC2 ..> UC4 : <<extend>>\n[contactForce > 5 N]
UC2 ..> UC5 : <<extend>>

note right of UC4
  Triggered automatically by
  SafetyModule  (no actor input).
  Maps to FSM: accept
  ForceThresholdExceeded
  then safetyHold
end note

note right of UC3
  Actor OR watchdog can trigger.
  Maps to FSM: accept
  EStopSignal / WatchdogTimeout
  then emergencyStop
end note

@enduml
